messages.content:
Task exclusion-402
SQLite schema:
CREATE TABLE accounts_402(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, active INTEGER); CREATE TABLE items_402(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, account_id INTEGER, amount INTEGER, status TEXT); CREATE TABLE blocks_402(account_id INTEGER);
Obligations: Return id, qualifying_count for active accounts that have at least one item, have NO item whose status is NULL or differs from ok, have NO item with NULL amount or amount < 46, and are not blocked. Each block with a non-NULL account_id blocks that account; NULL block entries block nobody. qualifying_count counts all items for each qualifying account. Order by id.
Public example data: {"accounts_402": [[747, 1], [204, 1], [465, 1], [394, 1], [743, 1], [770, 1], [436, 1], [629, 0], [600, 1]], "items_402": [[1, 204, 53, null], [2, 204, 59, "ok"], [3, 465, 58, "bad"], [4, 465, 64, "ok"], [5, 394, null, "ok"], [6, 394, 51, "ok"], [7, 743, 45, "ok"], [8, 743, 62, "ok"], [9, 770, 50, "ok"], [10, 770, 51, "ok"], [11, 436, 53, "ok"], [12, 436, 48, "ok"], [13, 629, 62, "ok"], [14, 629, 62, "ok"], [15, 600, 46, "ok"], [16, 600, 63, "ok"]], "blocks_402": [[null], [770], [770]]}
Write a reusable SQL query valid for all databases satisfying this schema and obligations, not just these example rows.

message.content:
{"action":"check","sql":"SELECT accounts_402.id, COUNT(items_402.id) AS qualifying_count FROM accounts_402 WHERE accounts_402.active = 1 AND accounts_402.id IN (SELECT DISTINCT items_402.account_id FROM items_402 WHERE items_402.status = 'ok' AND items_402.amount IS NOT NULL AND items_402.amount >= 46) AND accounts_402.id NOT IN (SELECT blocks_402.account_id FROM blocks_402 WHERE blocks_402.account_id IS NOT NULL) GROUP BY accounts_402.id ORDER BY accounts_402.id;"}

{"ok": false, "error": "no such column: items_402.id", "expected": [[436, 2], [600, 2]]}
